  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Ship of Opportunity: Canada to Japan - 1980-present",
  "description": "Data from merchant ships travelling between British Columbia and Japan, from 1980-1990 (Canada Ace), 1995 to 2000, continuing (Skaugran), and 1999-2000, continuing (Alligator Hope). Data collected include surface total carbon dioxide, alkalinity, nutrients, chlorophyll a, carbon-13 in seawater, and atmospheric carbon-13. Underway measurements include position, time, temperature and salinity. Skaugran samples and data were collected 3-4 times daily by scientific staff and once daily by ship`s engineers until 1999, then were reduced to daily engineer`s samples. Alligator Hope samples were collected 3 times daily.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Constructing models of North Pacific carbon cycling; air-sea exchange, monitoring long term changes in the North Pacific Ocean, tracking water masses in the ocean, El Nino monitoring\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Custodian will be leaving soon and has a large quantity of data not secured in a regional data centre. Risk of Loss: High Impact Justification: Time series of 5 to 10 years Impact of Loss: Medium Recommended Action: Obtain access to data, bring data to archives",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23628969",
