  "measurementTechnique": "Logical consistency: Interlaboratory comparisons of nutrient and carbon-13 and oxygen-18 measurements; comparison to known standards. Salinometer calibrated with standard seawater. Fluorometer calibrated with commercially prepared standard. Data are plotted to detect outlyers.\n\nCompleteness: Dataset Complications: Some CTD data from the Alligator Hope are questionable. Chlorophyll data may be questionable. Canada Ace data are of unknown quality, and therefore will not be released. No data collected 1991-1994. For some programs, fewer parameters were measured. Electronic Data Complications: Magnetic tapes are older than their guaranteed physical lifespan.\n\nProcessing step (1980): IOS and Japanese collaborators",
  "usageInfo": {
    "@type": "CreativeWork",
    "name": "Use and access constraints (from the FGDC record; no license is granted)",
    "text": "Use constraints: Collaborative data with Japanese scientists. The less recent data will be released after publication, with permission of the collaborators. Alkalinity and TCO2 data from the Canadian Ace have been sent to OSAP archives. Access constraints: Private Distribution liability: [unknown]"
  },
